{c: Verse 1}
[Gm] [F] [Bb] [Cm] [Gm],        My [Gm] mother came to Hazard
when I was just seven,        Even then the folks in town said
with [Bb] prejudised eyes,        That [C] boys not right
[Gm] Three years ago,        when I came to know Mary
First time that someone look beyond,        the [Bb] rumours and the lies
And saw the [C] man inside,        We [Eb] used to walk down by the [Bb] river
She [Eb] loved to watch the sun go [Gm] down,        We [Eb] used to walk along the [Gm] river
And [F] dream our [Eb] way out of this [Gm] town,        [Gm] No one understood
what I felt for Mary,        No one cared until the night
she went out [Bb] walking all alone,        And [C] never came home
[Gm] Man with the badge,        came knocking next morning
Here was I surrounded by,        a thousand [Bb] fingers suddenly
Pointing [C] right at me,        I [Eb] swear I left her by the [Bb] river
I [Eb] swear I left her safe and [Gm] sound,        I [Eb] need to [Bb] make it to the [Gm] river
And [F] leave this [Eb] old Nebraska [Gm] town,        [F] Thinkng about my life going by
[Eb] How its done me [Bb] wrong,        [F] Theres no escape for me this time
[Eb] All of my [Bb] rescue are,        [F] gone, long [Gm] gone
I [Eb] swear I left her by the [Bb] river,        I [Eb] swear I left her safe and [Gm] sound
I [Eb] need to [Bb] make it to the [Gm] river,        And [F] leave this [Eb] old Nebraska [Gm] town
